course: dictionary
lesson: 6730
title: Learning about a rare animal from clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you may never have seen. The clues in the sentences around them help you picture them. «The okapi is a shy animal that lives in the African forest.» Shy tells you it is not bold or noisy. It keeps away from people and hides.
explain: «The okapi is the giraffe's closest living relative.» You may not know relative, but giraffe is a clue. A relative is a member of the same family, like a cousin. So the okapi and the giraffe are related, even though they look different.
explain: Look for the detail that matters. «Its stripy legs break up its outline in the shadows.» Stripes help it hide, so you can work out why an animal might have them. When you are not sure, check your guess by reading the rest of the text.
fact: An okapi is a shy animal from the rainforests of the Democratic Republic of the Congo.
fact: The okapi is the giraffe's closest living relative, but it has a shorter neck and stripes on its legs like a zebra.
fact: Its stripes help it hide in light and shadow, which is called camouflage.
fact: «The okapi's long tongue can reach its own eyes and ears to clean them.»
fact: Okapis are endangered, because people hunt them and their forest is being cut down. Zoos and animal books sometimes call them the «forest giraffe».
exercise: «The okapi is a shy animal that lives in the forest.» What does shy mean here? | Brave and bold | Loud and fond of crowds | *Quiet and keeping away from people | Very tall
exercise: The okapi is the giraffe's closest living relative. What does relative mean? | A tree in the forest | *A member of the same family or group, like a cousin | A giraffe's enemy | A type of zebra
exercise: «Its stripy legs break up its outline in the shadows.» Find and copy the word that means dark patches where light does not reach. | light | legs | *shadows | stripes
test: «The okapi's long tongue can reach its own ears.» What is an okapi's tongue like? | Short and pink | Flat like a leaf | Soft and furry | *Long and dark
test: Why might the okapi's stripes help it? | To look bigger than other animals | To swim fast in rivers | To make a loud noise | *To hide in light and shadow in the forest
exam: Which sentence is a true fact about okapis? | The okapi lives in the desert | The okapi is a type of bird | The okapi has spots like a leopard | *The okapi is the giraffe's closest living relative
